<h1>shader_current</h1>
<p>This function will return the index ID value of the shader currently being used for rendering, or it will return -1 if no shader is being used.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">shader_current();</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Asset_Shader"><a target="_blank" href="../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Shaders.htm">Shader Asset</a></span> or -1 (if no shader is assigned)</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">if (shader_current() == -1)<br/>
{<br/>
    shader_set(sh_warp)<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code will check to see what the current shader is and if it returns -1 (no shader being used) then a shader is set.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
